# Pinned commit of github.com/mstan/psxrecomp (the shared framework) used to
# build this repo. Bumping this is a deliberate, reviewable change — psxrecomp
# is a separate repo evolving on its own cadence. Update via:
#   git -C ../psxrecomp rev-parse master > /tmp/sha && \
#     sed -i "s|^sha=.*|sha=$(cat /tmp/sha)|" psxrecomp-v4.pin
branch=feat/native-wide
sha=676ac99
# Bumped 2026-06-15 (native-wide FOV complete): psxrecomp feat/native-wide adds
# [widescreen.cull] auto_screen_x — a gen-time pass that auto-detects the GTE
# render-funnel screen-extent reject (sltiu 0x140/0x141 width paired with a
# sltiu 0xE0 height) and routes every WIDTH cull through psx_ws_x_margin(),
# sign-extended + shifted so BOTH 16:9 margins reveal. 4:3 byte-identical
# (margin 0). USER-VALIDATED: with game.toml auto_screen_x = true the revealed
# left+right margins fill with real geometry (no more 320-edge cull). One opt-in
# flag, ~106 sites auto-widened, generic to any PSX GTE title — supersedes the
# WIP "wtrace OT writers" plan in the checkpoint note below. Remaining polish
# (separate, non-blocking): load-in fade + pause gray-filter still drawn at 4:3.
# ---- prior pin (compositor checkpoint) ----
# Bumped 2026-06-15 (compositor checkpoint): psxrecomp feat/native-wide now
# carries the native-wide render-pipeline rewrite — a separate per-framebuffer
# WIDE COMPOSITOR surface (software renderer), canonical PSX VRAM left faithful
# (4:3 / non-opted = byte-identical). SW path works: 16:9 flicker fixed, faithful,
# terrain platform fills. WIP: discrete foreground objects + parallax backdrop
# still culled at the 4:3 edge (separate spawn path — wtrace OT writers next);
# GL compositor port pending. See psxrecomp/NATIVE_WIDE_PLAN.md + session handoff.
